import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Supported Image Formats | ConvertAnyFile" description="Learn which image formats ConvertAnyFile recognizes, which outputs are available, and important format limitations before converting.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Formats</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Format reference</span><h1>Choose the right image format for the job.</h1><p>Image conversion is the first live category on ConvertAnyFile. Runtime codec availability is checked before conversion, so the interface does not pretend a codec works when the browser engine cannot decode it.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="format-grid"><article class="format-card"><span>JPG</span><h3>Photos & compatibility</h3><p>Lossy photo format with very broad support. No alpha transparency.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>PNG</span><h3>Lossless graphics</h3><p>Useful for screenshots, graphics, and transparency. Often larger than JPG for photographs.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>WebP</span><h3>Modern web delivery</h3><p>Supports lossy or lossless workflows and transparency in modern browsers.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>AVIF</span><h3>High-efficiency images</h3><p>Modern compression format. Conversion support depends on the codec packaged with the runtime.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>HEIC</span><h3>Phone photography</h3><p>Common on Apple devices. Often converted to JPG or PNG for broader compatibility.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>TIFF</span><h3>Scanning & professional imaging</h3><p>Flexible container used in print, scanning, and archival workflows. Files can be large.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>GIF</span><h3>Legacy animation</h3><p>Widely recognized format with palette limitations. Animated source behavior can vary by target format.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>BMP</span><h3>Bitmap images</h3><p>Simple bitmap format that can be much larger than compressed delivery formats.</p></article><article class="format-card"><span>RAW</span><h3>Camera files</h3><p>Several camera extensions are recognized, but actual decoding depends on the runtime delegate and the specific camera file.</p></article></div><div class="callout"><strong>Support is capability-derived.</strong><p>File extension alone is not trusted. ConvertAnyFile checks file signatures first, then verifies the browser conversion engine before enabling runtime-dependent conversions.</p></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
